          "period": "2026-08-23",
          "status": "passed",
          "source": "focused xcodebuild measurement",
          "visualRole": "actual"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "evidence:facade-run",
      "@type": "Evidence",
      "title": "Complete optimized facade run passes",
      "content": "After the periodic-chart ownership correction and the generalized nonsingular-periodic analytic-pair lift, the complete optimized SwiftCADTests bundle passed 181/181 tests across 69 suites in 244.344 seconds. Public general torus-torus operations also pass independently in 41.254 to 46.624 seconds, and the public general cone-torus suite passes in 7.541 seconds without changing expected volumes or tolerances.",
      "epistemicStatus": "Verified",
      "confidence": 1,
      "source": "xcodebuild SwiftCAD-Tests xcresult summary",
      "sourceUrl": "file:///Users/1amageek/Library/Developer/Xcode/DerivedData/SwiftCAD-eygvayaohnarbvacofxtpbbgsqub/Logs/Test/Test-SwiftCAD-Tests-2026.08.23_09-44-42-+0900.xcresult",
      "reliability": 1,
      "supportsClaim": [
        "insight:release-not-ready"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "evidence:exchange-tests",
      "@type": "Evidence",
      "title": "Exchange behavior tests",
      "content": "CADExchangeTests compiles and passes 237/237 tests, including exact STEP/IGES round trips, same-parameter procedural surface exchange, USD subset behavior, resource limits, and typed rejection paths.",
      "epistemicStatus": "Verified",
      "confidence": 1,
      "source": "xcodebuild CADExchange-Tests xcresult summary",
      "sourceUrl": "file:///Users/1amageek/Library/Developer/Xcode/DerivedData/SwiftCAD-eygvayaohnarbvacofxtpbbgsqub/Logs/Test/Test-CADExchange-Tests-2026.08.23_09-51-04-+0900.xcresult",
      "reliability": 1,
      "supportsClaim": [
        "insight:constrained-usable"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "evidence:surface-gap",
      "@type": "Evidence",
      "title": "Residual supported surface-intersection mismatch",
      "content": "The dispatcher now resolves exact same-parameter representations before algorithm selection, so ruled surfaces intersect through exact rational B-splines while results retain the original surface identity and UV chart. General non-reducible procedural offsets still have no exact rational representation and remain outside the concrete representation-pair closure claimed by the supported surface-surface capability.",
      "epistemicStatus": "Verified",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "source": "KernelCapabilities+Geometry.swift, DefaultSurfaceSurfaceIntersector.swift, Surface3D+ExactSameParameterRepresentation.swift, and OffsetSurface3D.swift",
      "sourceUrl": "file:///Users/1amageek/Desktop/3D/swift-CAD/Sources/CADGeometry/DefaultSurfaceSurfaceIntersector.swift",
      "reliability": 0.99,
      "supportsClaim": [
        "insight:composition-root-blocker"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "evidence:boolean-path",
      "@type": "Evidence",
      "title": "Boolean composition path",
      "content": "The Boolean pipeline invokes the default surface-surface intersector for face pairs. The latest implementation correctly routes one non-contractible periodic closed component through an explicit-seam open arrangement and validates the resulting exact cylinder strip, removing the prior incomplete marker. The Boolean capability remains partial because broader representation pairs, doubly periodic arrangements, coincident cases, and downstream feature compositions are not yet closed by a same-revision behavioral matrix.",
      "epistemicStatus": "Verified",
      "confidence": 0.98,
      "source": "BooleanPipeline.swift and exact Boolean materializers",
      "sourceUrl": "file:///Users/1amageek/Desktop/3D/swift-CAD/Sources/CADKernel/BooleanPipeline.swift",
      "reliability": 0.98,
      "supportsClaim": [
        "insight:composition-root-blocker",
        "insight:general-not-achieved"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "evidence:periodic-boolean-progress",
      "@type": "Evidence",
      "title": "Essential periodic Boolean strip now materializes exactly",
      "content": "A full-period cylinder face with an explicit seam at a shifted chart coordinate is partitioned by an essential constant-v intersection curve into a finite strip. The focused production-path test passes arrangement, exact sewing, and ValidatedBRepModel exact validation. Companion tests accept only an opposite-orientation whole-period seam pair, reject an uncertified duplicate edge, and retain the upper endpoint lift when trimming a periodic pcurve.",
      "epistemicStatus": "Verified",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "source": "BooleanOpenFaceArrangementTests, PeriodicFaceSeamValidatorTests, and SurfaceParameterCurvePeriodicEvaluationTests",
      "sourceUrl": "file:///Users/1amageek/Desktop/3D/swift-CAD/Tests/CADKernelTests/BooleanOpenFaceArrangementTests.swift",
      "reliability": 0.99,
      "supportsClaim": [
        "insight:substrate-strong",
        "insight:constrained-usable"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "evidence:representation-closure-progress",
      "@type": "Evidence",
      "title": "Ruled surfaces now preserve exact identity through intersection and sewing",
      "content": "Focused current-worktree tests pass ruled-plane and ruled-ruled surface intersection through exact same-parameter rational B-spline representations, preserve the original UV chart across JSON round-trip, and consume the certified pcurve in a four-edge trim loop that sews and validates as an exact BRep face. B-spline closest-point projection now uses the same globally bounded interval branch-and-bound contract as procedural surfaces and returns typed resource failure when the proof budget cannot close the bound.",
      "epistemicStatus": "Verified",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "source": "SurfaceSurfaceIntersectionTests, BSplineSurfaceParameterProjectionTests, and ProceduralSurfaceKernelIntegrationTests",
      "sourceUrl": "file:///Users/1amageek/Desktop/3D/swift-CAD/Tests/CADGeometryTests/SurfaceSurfaceIntersectionTests.swift",
      "reliability": 0.99,
      "supportsClaim": [
        "insight:substrate-strong",
        "insight:constrained-usable"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "evidence:query-heuristic",
      "@type": "Evidence",
      "title": "Residual Agent query heuristics",
      "content": "B-spline surface closest-point queries now use globally bounded interval branch-and-bound projection. The public curve closest-point and general directional projection paths still use finite sampling and local Newton refinement, so the complete Agent selection/query surface is not globally certified.",
      "epistemicStatus": "Verified",
      "confidence": 0.98,
      "source": "CurveQueryEvaluator.swift",
      "sourceUrl": "file:///Users/1amageek/Desktop/3D/swift-CAD/Sources/CADKernel/CurveQueryEvaluator.swift",
